<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices ease, limited plant demand.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices ease, limited plant demand.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices eased by 200-250 rupees per tonne on Friday on limited demand from processing plants, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices fell sharply on heavy selling from plants and refineries against very little demand. Soyoil solvent was down by 300 rupees and soyoil refined by 400 rupees per tonne.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were steady in thin trade. Export demand fell and selling from Indian exporters was also limited. Soymeal yellow was $275-276 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $135-136 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,650 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,600-4,625 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
